        "comments": "The assembly keSacKowa6.1 is based on 35x PacBio data and Arima2 Hi-C data generated by the Wellcome Sanger Institute Tree of Life Programme (https://www.sanger.ac.uk/programme/tree-of-life/). The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi and OATK. Finally, the primary assembly was analysed and manually improved using TreeVal. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. A large number of centromeric repeats is in the unlocalised sequences. The exact order and orientation of the contigs on chromosome 5 (9.3 Mbp - 10.5 Mbp), chromosome 12 (6.0 Mbp - 6.9 Mbp) are unknown.",
